  "id": "COMPOUND:23337 - PROTEIN:3691",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Nanolobatin B may interact with Arginine deiminase through multiple indirect pathways. The drug target relationship is supported by three distinct paths, each linking Nanolobatin B to Arginine deiminase via different intermediaries. In Path 1, Nanolobatin B targets Cyclin-dependent kinase 7, which is a target of AT9283, and AT9283 targets Arginine deiminase. In Path 2, Nanolobatin B directly targets Isoleucine--tRNA ligase, which is a target of Lambertiainc Acid, also targeting Arginine deiminase. Path 3 similarly links Nanolobatin B to Isoleucine--tRNA ligase, which is a target of Calanphenanthrene A, also targeting Arginine deiminase. These pathways collectively indicate that Nanolobatin B may modulate Arginine deiminase through different molecular mechanisms, possibly by influencing upstream regulators or enzymes involved in the metabolic pathway. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, but the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain without further experimental validation.",
